# eas.json — release-infra, owned outside any single feature capability. This file is created by
# `npx expo install <native-module>` (it slipped in with `npx expo install expo-audio` during audio
# work) and by `npx eas-cli init`; README.md ("Not yet set up") records that adopting it is a team
# decision, not a per-person one, because it binds the repo to an Expo account/project. Ignored so
# a local copy needed for `eas build` isn't silently committed with a feature change. If/when the
# team decides to adopt EAS, delete this entry in the same change that adds the file back.
eas.json

